# sqlx embeds migration file bytes into the compiled binary at build time
# (sqlx::migrate!() in database/manager.rs) and verifies a checksum of that
# exact content against what's recorded in each database's _sqlx_migrations
# table. If Git rewrites these files' line endings (e.g. CRLF on Windows via
# core.autocrlf=true), the checksum changes and every existing install fails
# to start with "migration ... was previously applied but has been modified".
# Force LF so migrations stay byte-stable across platforms and checkouts.
frontend/src-tauri/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
